{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #1032: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. We say that a graph is $4$-chromatic critical if it has chromatic number $4$, and removing any edge decreases the chromatic number to $3$.\n\nIs there, for arbitrarily large $n$, a $4$-chromatic critical graph on $n$ vertices with minimum degree $\\gg n$? Current best: Toft conjectured that a $4$-chromatic critical graph on $n$ vertices has at least $(\\frac{5}{3}+o(1))n$ vertices, and has examples to show this would be the best possible. Prize: no. Tags: chromatic number, graph theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_3086f5d99f60a88b3a7bd8fa6f051efd36696ec3fff3123ec85ec94a99e416e3","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1032","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_91131c974ee815e2","object_root":"sha256:7ecfdc09d856fd5b9d1b8acbbbd205ff278fb094905065e8c1ccd8d18756b70c","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1032"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schem